{"kind":"stack","id":"magnets-poles","title":"Magnets: attract or repel?","theme":{"background":"#1e2a3a","foreground":"#f5f5f5","font":"Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Magnetic poles"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Every magnet has two ends called poles, a north pole and a south pole."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1-next","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1n-t","content":"Attract or repel"},{"type":"text","id":"c1n-e","content":"Attract means pull together. Repel means push apart."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Two north poles are placed facing each other. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"They push apart","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"They pull together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"They stick and do not move","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"A north pole and a south pole are placed facing each other. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"They pull together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"They push apart","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"They spin in a circle","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Two south poles are placed facing each other. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"They push apart","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"They pull together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"They stick together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"You find two magnets on the table. Which will you try first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Turn one magnet around","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Hold them close, same ends","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You turn one magnet around. Now the ends face each other and they snap together. Nice find!"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You hold the same ends together and they push apart. Try the other way round next time!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which pair of poles will attract each other?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"North and south","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"North and north","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"South and south","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"A magnet is placed near a paper clip. The magnet pulls the clip towards it. What does this show?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"The magnet attracts the clip","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"The magnet repels the clip","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"The clip makes the magnet heavier","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Two magnets are placed with a north pole facing a south pole. Which word describes what they will do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Attract","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Repel","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Melt","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-q","content":"You want two magnets to push each other away. Which poles should face each other?"},{"type":"button","id":"c11-a","label":"Two north poles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-b","label":"A north pole and a south pole","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-c","label":"A magnet and a paper clip","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c12","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c12-h","content":"Magnets finished: attract or repel!"},{"type":"text","id":"c12-m","content":"Well done. You can now predict how magnets will behave."}],"actions":[]}}
